---
import ProfileToc from '../../components/ProfileToc.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { publicEntries, formatDate } from '../../utils/content';

const actors:any[] = await publicEntries('actors');
const campaigns:any[] = await publicEntries('campaigns');
const malware:any[] = await publicEntries('malware');
const tools:any[] = await publicEntries('tools');
const sources:any[] = await publicEntries('sources');
const updates:any[] = await publicEntries('updates');
const aliases = actors.reduce((sum, actor:any) => sum + actor.data.aliases.length, 0);
const latest = [...updates].sort((left:any, right:any) => {
  const byDate = +new Date(right.data.date) - +new Date(left.data.date);
  return byDate || left.data.slug.localeCompare(right.data.slug);
})[0];
const stats = [
  ['Actors', actors.length],
  ['Aliases', aliases],
  ['Campaigns', campaigns.length],
  ['Malware', malware.length],
  ['Tools', tools.length],
  ['Sources', sources.length]
];
const sections = [
  { slug: 'purpose', text: 'Purpose' },
  { slug: 'coverage-roadmap', text: 'Coverage and review' },
  { slug: 'public-records', text: 'Public records and reuse' },
  { slug: 'boundaries', text: 'Boundaries' },
  { slug: 'editorial-approach', text: 'Editorial accountability' }
];
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Purpose, audience, ownership, maintenance and limitations of APT Notes by HECAVEX.">
  <article class="shell about-shell">
    <header class="about-head">
      <div class="about-summary">
        <p class="eyebrow">APT Notes / About</p>
        <h1>Source-backed threat actor research.</h1>
        <p class="lead">APT Notes preserves publisher-specific attribution, operational context and uncertainty as connected public research records.</p>
        <p>It is built for analysts, defenders, investigators, journalists and researchers who need to move from a name to the evidence behind it.</p>
        <div class="about-actions"><a class="button" href="/actors/">Browse actor dossiers →</a><a href="/about/methodology/">Read methodology →</a></div>
      </div>

      <dl class="project-facts" aria-label="APT Notes project status">
        <div><dt>Purpose</dt><dd>Preserve source-specific actor, campaign and capability claims as linked research records.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Audience</dt><dd>Threat-intelligence analysts, defenders, investigators, journalists and researchers.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Owner</dt><dd><a href="https://hecavex.com/en/about/">Deividas Lis / HECAVEX</a></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Maintenance</dt><dd><span class="badge current">Maintained</span> Best effort; no monitoring or response SLA.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Last meaningful update</dt><dd>{latest ? <><time datetime={latest.data.date.toISOString()}>{formatDate(latest.data.date)}</time><br /><a href={`/updates/#${latest.data.slug}`}>{latest.data.title}</a></> : 'No public updates yet'}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Security and corrections</dt><dd><a href="/security/">Security policy</a> · <a href="https://hecavex.com/en/contact/">Editorial contact</a></dd></div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <div class="stat-grid about-stats" aria-label="Public APT Notes catalogue statistics">
      {stats.map(([name, count]) => <div class="stat"><strong>{count}</strong><span>{name}</span></div>)}
    </div>

    <div class="profile-grid about-grid">
      <ProfileToc items={sections} contextLabel="On this page" title="About APT Notes" ariaLabel="About APT Notes sections" />
      <div class="prose profile-body about-body">
        <section id="purpose">
          <h2>Purpose</h2>
          <p>APT Notes is a source-driven intelligence catalogue for searching, filtering and pivoting between selected threat actors, aliases, campaigns, malware, tools, targeting, techniques and attribution claims.</p>
          <p>Depth is prioritised over directory size. APT Notes does not attempt to reproduce every actor record already available elsewhere. A profile is published only when HECAVEX can preserve source-specific attribution, meaningful operational context and an explicit review history.</p>
          <p>It is a separate product from <a href="https://hecavex.com/en/research/">HECAVEX Research ↗</a>, which remains the publication for long-form investigations, analysis and commentary.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="coverage-roadmap">
          <h2>Coverage and review</h2>
          <p>Coverage expands one dossier at a time. Priority is given to actors relevant to European and Baltic security, actors connected to current HECAVEX research, and records where public naming or attribution requires careful separation.</p>
          <p>Published profiles are reviewed at least annually. After 180 days a record is marked review due; after 365 days it is marked stale until reassessed. A stale label describes review age, not actor inactivity.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="public-records">
          <h2>Public records and reuse</h2>
          <p>Public actor metadata is available as versioned static JSON. Use the <a href="/api/actors.json">actor index</a>, the JSON link on an individual profile, or the cross-project <a href="https://labs.hecavex.com/data/">HECAVEX data catalogue</a>. The <a href="/licence/">data licence and attribution boundary</a> applies to reuse. These exports are research records, not a live blocklist or operational feed.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="boundaries">
          <h2>Boundaries</h2>
          <p class="callout">APT Notes is not a live threat feed, detection service, SIEM, vulnerability scanner, authoritative attribution body or replacement for MITRE ATT&amp;CK.</p>
          <p>Its public-source coverage is selective, reporting can be incomplete and actor boundaries can change. A record describes the evidence available at its review date; it does not claim exhaustive visibility.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="editorial-approach">
          <h2>Editorial accountability</h2>
          <p>Source claims are separated from APT Notes assessments. Alias overlap is represented explicitly, uncertainty is retained, and corrections appear in the public change history.</p>
          <p>Security concerns and corrections have a published route, while methodology and licensing remain inspectable without an account.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="about-next" aria-labelledby="about-next-title">
      <div class="section-head"><h2 id="about-next-title">Continue into the evidence</h2></div>
      <div class="grid">
        <a class="panel" href="/actors/"><strong>Browse dossiers</strong><br /><span>Open actor records →</span></a>
        <a class="panel" href="/about/methodology/"><strong>Inspect methodology</strong><br /><span>Review the editorial rules →</span></a>
        <a class="panel" href="/licence/"><strong>Reuse public data</strong><br /><span>Read the licence boundary →</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
